# Tools the repo's own tooling shells out to. Every entry is justified by a real
# call site, so the list stays reviewable rather than a guess. This file is data,
# not a script: one tool per line, `#` comments and blank lines ignored, and it
# deliberately carries no shebang and no executable bit.
#
# Two lints consume it, closing the drift in both directions:
# - .ci/check-devshell-provides: every entry here must be provided by the flake
#   devShell, and every package the devShell declares must contribute at least
#   one entry here (or be excluded by name, with a reason).
# - .ci/check-tool-declarations: every tool named by a
#   `commands::*executable_exists` call site under .ci/, .githooks/, or the
#   repo-root runners must appear here.
#
# Deliberately absent:
# - prettier, yamlfmt, taplo, nixfmt, mdformat: treefmt resolves these from the
#   Nix store directly, never through PATH.
# - lychee, kcov: invoked by CI actions, not by any script in this repo.
# - zizmor: invoked from zizmor.yml's run block through .ci/in-devshell, so the
#   devShell must provide it, but no script in this repo names it.
# - flatpak, appman, apt, dnf, pacman, pwgen, bc and friends: invoked by
#   scripts/, which is the repo's payload rather than its tooling. Those are
#   expected to come from the machine.
#
# Entries are alphabetical; each carries the call site that warrants it.

# invoked directly by .ci/run-lint-checks
actionlint
# run-tests invokes bats from PATH; the flake devShell provides it
bats
# invoked by .ci/check-jsonschema
check-jsonschema
# invoked by .githooks/commit-msg to validate the prospective commit message
commitlint
# invoked directly by .ci/run-lint-checks
editorconfig-checker
# run-tests' default `bats --jobs` path dies without flock
flock
# asserted by the .ci/check-* workflow lints
gawk
# asserted by .ci/apply-repo-settings
gh
# every repo-tooling script derives REPO_DIR via `git rev-parse`
git
# asserted by the .ci/check-* workflow lints
jq
# the task runner the .justfile and README document
just
# invoked directly by .ci/run-lint-checks
markdownlint-cli2
# invoked by .ci/build-site, which the `docs` recipe, the lint suite, and the
# Pages workflow all call
mkdocs
# asserted by .ci/check-devshell-provides and .ci/check-flake-eval-warnings
nix
# run-tests' default `bats --jobs` path needs GNU parallel
parallel
# the check-scripts / shellcheck-scripts gate
shellcheck
# the check-scripts gate, and shell_scripts::find shells out to `shfmt --find`
shfmt
# invoked directly by .ci/run-lint-checks
typos
# invoked directly by .ci/run-lint-checks
yamllint
# asserted by the .ci/check-* workflow lints
yq
